# Media does not live in the repository. CLAUDE.md §5 says a photograph the
# site can use is a Media Library record on object storage, not a file on disk,
# and the same is true of video: a 4K master is a master, not something a
# browser should ever download. `public/images/` holds web-delivery renditions
# only — named `<id>-web-<width>x<height>.mp4` so the name says what the file
# is — and the masters they came from sit in storage, untracked.
/storage/app/video-masters
/storage/app/seed-video

# Master containers and master-shaped names, wherever they land. A rendition is
# never called any of these, so nothing shippable matches.
*.mov
*.mkv
*.avi
*.mxf
*-uhd_*.mp4
*_3840_2160_*.mp4
*_2880_1440_*.mp4
*_2160p*.mp4
*-master.mp4

# There is no size rule in gitignore, so the size limit is a test:
# tests/Feature/RepositoryWeightTest.php fails if any tracked file passes it.
